From: forge build <64113367+renownitall@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Derive the checkbox corner radius from the CornerRadius setting

Upstream hardcodes checkBoxCornerRadius to 6 and never updates it from
settings, so non-circle checkboxes keep a 6px rounding even with
CornerRadius=0. Halving matches the other secondary radii
(menuItemBorderRadius, listViewItemBorderRadius) and preserves the
default rendering exactly (12 / 2 = 6).

--- a/src/config.cpp
+++ b/src/config.cpp
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@ void Config::onSettingsChanged() {
     listViewItemBorderRadius = settingsCornerRadius / 2;
     controlsCornerRadius = settingsCornerRadius;
     tabCornerRadius = settingsCornerRadius;
+    checkBoxCornerRadius = settingsCornerRadius / 2;
 
     circleCheckBox = settings->circleCheckBox();
     animationSpeed = settings->animationSpeed();
